{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792173850,"nonce":"G2o76szrbswQE7rsU9nX1tJwdLs=","title":"A runtime cast error inside a closure called through an anonymous-struct field is not caught: interp and hybrid abort","message":"Reported by the chimpmonk session; reproduced here on the shared release binary (ash 0.1.8, 2026-10-16).\n\nAn error raised by the runtime itself, a failed dynamic cast of a Haxe Array\u003cInt\u003e to Array\u003cFloat\u003e, inside a closure that is stored in a field of an anonymous structure and called from inside a try, is never caught. The process prints the error and aborts:\n\n    [ash] uncaught exception: \"Can't cast hl.types.ArrayBytes_Int to hl.types.ArrayBytes_Float\"\n    hlp_throw called without active trap; aborting\n    === CRASH: SIGABRT (signal 6) ...\n\nReproducer (haxe -main ClosureCastRepro -hl closure.hl; ash --quiet closure.hl):\n\n    typedef Command = {run:Dynamic-\u003eDynamic};\n    class ClosureCastRepro {\n      static function call(c:Command, args:Dynamic):Dynamic {\n        try { return c.run(args); } catch (e:Dynamic) { return \"caught \" + Std.string(e); }\n      }\n      static function main() {\n        var args:Dynamic = {v: [0, 90, 0]};\n        var convert:Command = {run: a -\u003e { var d:Array\u003cFloat\u003e = a.v; return d[1] * 2.0; }};\n        Sys.println(call(convert, args));\n      }\n    }\n\nExpected: \"caught Can't cast hl.types.ArrayBytes_Int to hl.types.ArrayBytes_Float\".\n\nBy mode: --mode interp and --mode hybrid abort; --mode jit prints the expected line. So it is in the interpreter's path, not the compiled tiers.\n\nWhat the reporter isolated: the same cast in a plain static function called inside the try is caught; a Haxe `throw new SomeClass()` from the same kind of struct-held closure is caught, with a typed catch and with Dynamic; arrays from haxe.Json.parse (ArrayDyn) do not trigger it, only ArrayBytes_Int does. So a throw raised by a runtime native (the dynamic-cast path) inside a closure that the interpreter runs through a dynamic or virtual field call does not find the trap that the enclosing try should give it.\n\nImpact: chimpmonk's editor runs agent commands as struct-held closures inside a try; a Haxe Array\u003cInt\u003e argument killed the process instead of returning a refusal. The reporter works around it by converting number arrays to Array\u003cFloat\u003e first, so nothing is blocked.\n\nNot started. Next step: find where the interpreter runs a closure called through a virtual field (the closure-runner callbacks) and whether the native that throws runs with a trap armed there.","files":null}]}